The political variables in Figure \ref{fig:politic1} are largely free of high 
correlations among them. The exception is the strong relationship between the 
number of incumbents running and the overall share of all candidates running 
who are incumbents -- two attempts at measuring the phenomenon of how open the 
election is. 


