The story is the same for policy measures in Figure \ref{fig:policy1}. The only 
large correlations are between reading and math state standardized assessment 
proficiency rates, a measure of academic performance of the district. Other high 
positive correlations occur between the success, failure, and attempts at passing 
bond or revenue limit override referenda. Curiously, superintendent turnover in 
year t-1 and year t is also highly correlated. 

